  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "Use the constant from wsutil/epochs.h for Un*x epoch to Y2K",
  "description": "Several protocols use the time since Jan 1 2000 UTC as an epoch\ncalculation. Replace the number with the constant from wsutil/epochs.h\nThese are mostly used to set the values of nstime_t secs / time_t,\nwhich are usually 64-bit these days, but many of the protocols were\nnot treating this as a 64-bit integer. OSS-Fuzz found a case where\nthis caused unnecessary overflow, due to casting to time_t only after\nadding two ints.\n\nOSS-Fuzz 513102817\n\nAI-Assisted: no",
  "state": "merged",
